WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.680
The Marvel Cinematic Universe has had plenty
of highs over the past decade, like "Avengers:

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.630
Endgame," and the occasional lows.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.549
"I better get my pants."

00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:16.129
But there's one universal truth that every
single fan can get behind: Miss Minutes is

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:17.700
brilliant in "Loki."

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.660
The mascot/A.I. helps run the Time Variance
Authority, also known as the TVA.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.070
She also charmed viewers from the instant
she was introduced.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.010
Loki first sees the animated character in
the informational videos playing in the TVA's

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.150
waiting area.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.620
Basically, Miss Minutes is a splash of brilliant
creativity in the cosmic bureaucracy that

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.150
makes the idea of the TVA go down a little
easier for audiences in the series' first

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.150
episode.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.489
However, many viewers of the show quickly
deduced that there is much more to Miss Minutes

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:45.820
than meets the eye.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.140
Towards the beginning of the show's sixth
episode, the adorable clock is revealed to

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.320
have a direct line to the man behind the curtain,
He Who Remains.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.921
When Loki and Sylvie manage to enchant their
way into the Citadel at the end of Time, Miss

00:00:56.921 --> 00:01:00.649
Minutes revels in offering the pair everything
they've ever wanted in exchange for taking

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:01.990
over the TVA.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:06.330
Miss Minutes might be some kind of virtual
A.I., but she's clearly got a devilish side

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.420
— something she's likely inherited from
He Who Remains.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.680
The script originally gave Miss Minutes much
more to do in the season finale.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.240
In fact, she was supposed to fight Loki and
Sylvie when they arrived in the citadel.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.780
Unfortunately, the closest viewers actually
got to seeing a battle with Miss Minutes was

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.320
a jump scare and a couple of quickly drawn
weapons.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.720
"Hey, Y'all."

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.590
But how exactly would a fight scene work in
this context?

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:34.300
It's not clear how Miss Minutes can affect
the real world, although we did see Loki try

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:38.230
unsuccessfully to swat her with a magazine
in the second episode of the season.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:41.930
Director Kate Herron opened up about the cute,
yet sinister, character to Marvel.com.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.180
She explained…

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:47.259
"Early on in the scripts, we all were definitely
united on, 'We've got to keep Miss Minutes

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:48.420
in the story somehow.'"

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.159
The director pointed out that she tempts both
of the variants with all they've ever wanted.

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:55.210
"That devil on the shoulder and trying to
tempt both Loki and Sylvie.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.940
It was fun that you got a sense of there's
something a bit more sinister going on here

00:01:58.940 --> 00:01:59.940
with her."

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.290
"You want the Infinity Gauntlet?

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.110
Yours.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:05.810
Throne of Asgard?

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.509
No problem."

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:10.610
And according to Herron, Miss Minutes almost
had a bigger role in the finale.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.069
"We always had a version where [Loki and Sylvie]
kept meeting her at the Citadel.

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:17.110
At one point, we had a fight scene with Miss
Minutes in the Citadel."

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:21.980
Because much of "Loki" Episode 6 was dedicated
to He Who Remains explaining exactly who he

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.722
is in exposition-heavy monologues, it's easy
to see why the focus was on the new villain.

00:02:25.722 --> 00:02:27.060
"We're all villains here."

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.760
Still, it's obvious that there are plenty
of fans who would like to see more of Miss

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.069
Minutes in the future.

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:35.700
And it's easy to speculate about the character
and her role in both the TVA and the Marvel

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.250
Multiverse as a whole.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.239
Now that the season finale of "Loki" has blown
the doors off the Sacred Timeline, who is

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:44.290
to say that we won't see an expanded role
for the charming A.I.?

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:48.320
Considering her connections to He Who Remains,
we wouldn't be shocked if she's full of previously

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:51.230
unheard information about the TVA and the
Multiverse.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.850
So, even if Miss Minutes doesn't get more
screen time on "Loki," there's certainly room

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.950
for a cameo in another Marvel project.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.349
With Season 2 on the way, it would be criminal
for Miss Minutes to not return, so here's

00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:04.760
hoping she finally gets a fight scene in the
next batch of episodes.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.800
If that's not in the cards, don't fret.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.080
There's too much love for her from the show's
creators to ignore the potential for another

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.080
appearance.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.800
Even if she isn't a focal point of a branching
timeline, she knows enough to cross over to

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.680
another world, just as she has into the hearts
of Marvel fans.

